                    ["AWS Bedrock Managed Models", "Bedrock states that prompts and completions are not used to train AWS models or shared with model providers for training; verify the exact managed offering rather than extending this to unrelated marketplace services.", "Standard managed inference is documented as not storing or logging prompts and completions by default; customer-enabled invocation logging persists them separately. Verify current model/service exceptions instead of inventing a universal thirty-day abuse-log period.", "Capture Bedrock service terms, model availability, region and inference-profile scope, plus evidence that payload logging and persistent features are disabled or compatible. Treat this as route-specific no-retention evidence, not an OpenAI-style ZDR approval process.", "Cross-region inference violates the promised location, invocation logs export content to storage, or fallback calls a model publisher directly under different terms."],
                    ["Google Cloud Vertex AI", "Customer data is not used to train or fine-tune managed models without permission or instruction; inspect model-specific terms, especially partner models and optional connected services.", "Certain models or account arrangements can involve prompt logging for abuse monitoring, with published periods such as up to thirty days. Eligibility and exceptions vary; inspect the current account and model terms rather than assigning one Vertex-wide default.", "Verify whether the exact account/model is exempt from abuse-monitoring retention or requires an approved exception. Review caching, grounding, session history, and request-response logging independently; restrict the route to features whose documented retention matches the contract.", "Fallback switches to a different API product, partner model, region, or grounding feature whose retention terms were never evaluated."],
